    {
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 11 },
      "id": 6,
      "options": {
        "content": "## If these panels are empty\n\nWork through this in order - it isolates the layer that is broken.\n\n1. **Did k6 send anything?** Prometheus should list k6 series:\n   [http://localhost:9090/api/v1/label/__name__/values](http://localhost:9090/api/v1/label/__name__/values)\n   If that has no `k6_*` names, the problem is on the k6 side: the output extension\n   is not enabled. `K6_PROMETHEUS_RW_SERVER_URL` only says *where* to send;\n   `K6_OUT=experimental-prometheus-rw` (k6 0.x) is what enables sending at all.\n2. **Is the target endpoint up?** [http://localhost:9090/targets](http://localhost:9090/targets)\n   and check the Prometheus container log for remote-write rejections. The receiver\n   needs `--web.enable-remote-write-receiver`.\n3. **Is this datasource the right one?** See Connections -> Data sources:\n   it must point at `http://prometheus:9090` from inside the compose network.\n4. **Is the time range right?** A run that finished 40 minutes ago is invisible if\n   the dashboard is looking at the last 5 minutes. Widen it, or use the k6 test's\n   `started_at` from `results/<run>/meta.json`.\n5. **Did the run flushes land?** k6 pushes every ~5s and once more at the end of\n   the test, so a run of a few seconds can produce very few samples.\n\nThis dashboard is a diagnostic, not a report. For the full set of k6 panels, import\nGrafana.com dashboard **19665** (k6 Prometheus) and pick the `prometheus` datasource.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Troubleshooting: no data in Grafana",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
